## INTRODUCTION
Metal−organic frameworks $\left(\mathrm{MOFs}\right)^{1-4}$ are porous crystalline materials displaying unique remarkable features that translate into a large number of applications5 such as gas storage and sheaprvareastiongn,/6 tlraar-nesnpeorgt,y coantvaelyrsiso,n8 0chweamtiecral smeendsiantgi,o9 l1i1ghotrdrug delivery.12 MOFs stand out for high and tunable surface areas and pore sizes as well as for dispersed active sites and functionalities within such porosity. These factors lead to a very rich host−guest chemistry,1 where the interactions
