## Biographies
Marta Viciano-Chumillas was born in Valencia (Spain) in 1980. She holds a postdoctoral fellow in the Coordination Chemistry Group at the University of Valencia. Her research interests focus on the design of novel biocompatible porous materials.
Marta Mon was born in Cheste (Valencia, Spain) in 1987. She holds a postdoctoral position at the $\mathrm{ITQ}$ UPV-CSIC, where she focuses on the study of the catalytic properties of MOFs.
Jesus Ferrando-Soria was born in Catadau (Valencia, Spain) in 1984. He currently holds a postdoctoral “Lacaixa Junior Leader” position at the University of Valencia. His research interests focus on the design and applications of functional porous materials.
Avelino Corma is a Professor at the ITQ (UPV-CSIC). He received his Ph.D. at the Complutense University of Madrid in 1976 and performed his Postdoc at Queen’s University. His main research field is heterogeneous catalysis.
Antonio Leyva-Pérez was born in Sevilla (Spain) in 1974. He is a Distinguished Researcher at the $\mathrm{ITQ}_{}$ UPV-CSIC, in Valencia (Spain). His research activity concerns the design and synthesis of catalysts for sustainable industrial reactions.
Donatella Armentano was born in Cosenza (Italy) in 1972. She is an Associate Professor at the University of Calabria where she focuses on the elucidation of the crystal structures of complex host−guest materials.
Emilio Pardo was born in Valencia (Spain) in 1977. He is an Associate Professor at the Universitat de València. His research interests focus on the design of novel examples of functional MOFs and their application in catalysis and environmental remediation.
